  "notes": "{跨|また}ぐ describes stepping over something or straddling it with legs apart.\n\nCONJUGATION (godan verb):\n- {跨|また}ぐ (dictionary form)\n- {跨|また}がない (negative)\n- {跨|また}いだ (past)\n- {跨|また}いで (te-form)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japanese culture, it is considered rude to step over people or their belongings. The concept of {跨|また}ぐ carries cultural significance regarding respect for others.",
